WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.717
(gentle music)

00:00:02.717 --> 00:00:07.447
- [Voiceover] This colorful
spot has a dark past.

00:00:07.447 --> 00:00:10.158
Las Palmitas was once a dangerous place

00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:13.679
with clashes between rival gangs.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.667
But the city government
launched and funded

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.524
a project called Pachuca Paints Itself

00:00:18.524 --> 00:00:20.941
to turn the community around.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.884
The painting itself involved participation

00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:28.134
from all of the households.

00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:36.639
They painted over 200 houses
using 5000 gallons of paint.

00:00:41.188 --> 00:00:42.880
These individually painted houses

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.092
combine to make one
beautiful rainbow design

00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:49.583
inspired by Pachuca's
nickname, La Bella Airosa,

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:52.083
or the beautiful, breezy city.

00:00:53.909 --> 00:00:56.869
The aim of the project was to
bring a sense of liveliness

00:00:56.869 --> 00:00:59.852
and livability back to the city.

00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:01.872
The Ministry of Planning and Evaluation

00:01:01.872 --> 00:01:03.220
of the City of Pachuca

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.361
has noted that the crime rate
in the city has decreased

00:01:06.361 --> 00:01:08.694
since the mural was painted.

